# Remotes over HTTPS: checked spec

A remote whose URL is `https://<host>/v1/<project>` is served by the DEUS Worker
([`platform/worker/`](../../platform/worker), D164), the only thing that touches the private
`deus-codebases` bucket. Each operation of the `Remote` ability is one request, so a thread needs
one allowed domain and, to write, one API key (`$DEUS_API_KEY`) instead of R2 credentials.

| `Remote` op | Request | Write scope |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `list` | `GET /bundles`, one name per line | none |
| `get` | `GET /bundles/<level>-<sha256>`, gzipped | none |
| `put` | `PUT /bundles/<name>`; 200 if it is already there | `push` |
| `delete` | `DELETE /bundles/<name>` (compaction, D73) | `compact` |
| `keys` | `GET /files/<folder>/`, one key per line | none |
| `download` | `GET /files/<key>` | none |
| `upload`, `drop` | `PUT`, `DELETE /files/<key>` | the folder: `assets`, `inbox`, `site` or `events` |
| `writeAll` | one `PUT /files/site/…` per file, 16 at a time | `site` |

The Worker checks that a pushed bundle decompresses to text whose SHA-256 is its name. Keys live in
the Worker's D1 database as the SHA-256 of their secret, with scopes and projects; `admin` implies
every scope and also manages keys at `/v1/keys`. `scripts/deus-keys.mjs` makes, lists and revokes
keys through the account's Cloudflare token.

The Worker half is checked in vitest (`src/worker-remote.test.ts`: scopes, revoked and expired keys,
the bundle hash, folder scopes, key management), and the whole path by `moon run deus-lang:remote-test`,
which pushes, pulls and publishes an explorer through the Worker on local workerd.

## Extensions

| Term | URI |
| --- | --- |
| `api` | `org.dxos.deus.api@1.0` |

## APIs

```mdl
api A-1: remotes and their handlers
  signatures:
  - Replicate.http : Text -> Text -> (Unit -> {Remote, IO | e} a) -> {IO | e} a
  - Replicate.bucket : Text -> Text -> Text -> Text -> (Unit -> {Remote, IO | e} a) -> {IO | e} a
  - Replicate.directory : Text -> (Unit -> {Remote, IO | e} a) -> {IO | e} a
  - Cli.withRemote : Text -> Text -> (Unit -> {Remote, IO, Throw Text} a) -> {IO, Throw Text} a
  - Cli.defaultRemote : Text -> Text -> {IO} Option Text
```
